    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 164,
        "text": "Welcome, everyone. Today we compare three sources about urban farming. Let's start with the city report. It has clear numbers, but it only covers one district.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "9ceaf630a66bf749adb72810edf46dc2087d8dac87b487c7141c04b92cdff7d3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 171,
        "sourceEnd": 242,
        "text": "Sorry, can I check? The report covers one district, not the whole city?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "99bbe9c8c94017f496546b93e52c0e8214b47a62257eea55f13e6464209491a2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 249,
        "sourceEnd": 370,
        "text": "Yes, only the north district. Next, the university study. It interviewed fifty families, but all of them were volunteers.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "cc2be5299649f115202718148b3f6fac70900c586b21acf418e3a2340609e6e7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 377,
        "sourceEnd": 417,
        "text": "So the study is detailed but not random?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "1c4cc7d352e8a681d9bf42d10447144c5f99d9a7ffc00c26c0dcb96510ff1305",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 424,
        "sourceEnd": 506,
        "text": "Exactly. Finally, the online article. It is easy to read, but it gives no sources.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "39726f993451c64757561833f1c6f4662eec8687ae72d14525bb8296a966626b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 513,
        "sourceEnd": 554,
        "text": "Wait, I thought it had a list at the end.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "24b8bb7320778d78505f41121773165e6770af3b04a15bd30bfa51f10a4986f0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 561,
        "sourceEnd": 712,
        "text": "No, I checked twice. No list. So each source has a different limitation. The report is narrow, the study is not random, and the article is unsupported.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "2b68c4ab4fe1ab7928182b53f20036dc3dd7fc0f1ab652cac51d89c882b507f4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 719,
        "sourceEnd": 752,
        "text": "Then how do we use them together?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "86f7c3a3a163ba1ea398f872ebeaaac8066bdeefdb5d0a79f71e0a0434b96e68",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 759,
        "sourceEnd": 913,
        "text": "We can use the report for local numbers, the study for family experiences, and the article only for background. But we must not treat any one as complete.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "33323d0246fe9f123a1532e4fe98a83c9b51e79516719439cdd5adf2a603e767",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 920,
        "sourceEnd": 955,
        "text": "What if we need a city-wide number?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "8d49a2005048f87db98f15e0c1e2586d2ed81777cf819d0781774a3dca8c8d42",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 962,
        "sourceEnd": 1053,
        "text": "Then we need a fourth source, like a national survey. The three we have cannot answer that.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "a2618cd1a506d424ea4a1cabf58f5906557620c875567a4a616e6af03b6659e8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1060,
        "sourceEnd": 1200,
        "text": "Okay. So the report is useful but limited in area. The study is useful but limited in sample. The article is useful but limited in evidence.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "e83d3ad7f2bf002f90f57a67a1367a6ff6e3b18144d5c4c2beb3e41bcbf9dfcb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1207,
        "sourceEnd": 1385,
        "text": "Good summary. Now, let's write our comparison in simple sentences and complex sentences. Use simple sentences for clear facts, and complex sentences for conditions and contrasts.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "304e5c7dd7d8bab8cf1c32f268a142b56cb86444516570f5493f000dc68794bd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1392,
        "sourceEnd": 1480,
        "text": "For example, \"Although the report is narrow, it gives exact numbers.\" That's a contrast.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "136f402cb14543c981e88d1c56b20f9a16563d209f57c44f4ac1ca4833ee96c1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1487,
        "sourceEnd": 1573,
        "text": "Yes. And \"If we need city-wide data, we must find another source.\" That's a condition.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "6ab63060c4bc34c47b130e484109793f611247f66b6941eed7d05f1561b63b91",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1580,
        "sourceEnd": 1678,
        "text": "What about cause? \"Because the study used volunteers, the results may not represent all families.\"",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "808316a5abd8110cec6bb6d17fda7344469088c83e15bb0e8ccd6fe4dd5b72c3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1685,
        "sourceEnd": 1931,
        "text": "Perfect. Now, punctuation: use a comma after a dependent clause when it comes first. \"Although the report is narrow, it gives exact numbers.\" No comma when the dependent clause comes second: \"The report gives exact numbers although it is narrow.\"",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "7b44f3f22cd276410b009edb7894a20add4ea150c8dee0e35862668f4c549391",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1938,
        "sourceEnd": 2013,
        "text": "Got it. So we mix simple and complex sentences, and we punctuate carefully.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "bfbbe7c809324b63e4fc4ac29feca7dcbfa581202ba198b15b5bbe419b570ad1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2020,
        "sourceEnd": 2067,
        "text": "Exactly. Let's practice with our three sources.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "6a34c27e1c1900cb462e1092e7bf6fcf6f2eb63a963e995dafedca2b7506ce93",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
